WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.800
The bandit's dilemma.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:11.833
The tutor can quiz you in four styles. Each one helps you remember with some probability, but the tutor doesn't know which is best.

3
00:00:11.833 --> 00:00:17.833
Here are the true values, hidden from the agent. Explain-in-your-own-words is best, at seventy percent.

4
00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:22.900
A greedy agent always uses whatever looks best so far.

5
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:35.600
It locked onto the first style that paid off, and never tried the others again. Early luck became a permanent mistake.

6
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:51.067
Now the agent tries a random style one time in ten. Its estimates sharpen, and it ends up using explain-it most. Exploration pays.

7
00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:59.967
Regret counts the reward lost compared with always using the best style. Greedy's regret keeps climbing. With exploration it flattens out.

8
00:00:59.967 --> 00:01:08.633
UCB explores smarter: it adds a bonus to styles it has rarely tried, so it explores where it's unsure, not at random.

